From c8cee803ef1038ee55bcddbe7347b7cbeffb9fed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Macready <william.macready@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:20:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(plan): step-aware axiswise masks (Lean side)

A where mask in a scan STEP statement or per-step intermediate now sees the
live scan coordinate(s) of its enclosing scan, on the reference evaluator and
the checked plan alike. RawAxiswisePlan gains maskContextRank (default 0): the
block context is appended after the tensor coordinates, checked against the
enclosing block's context rank (maskContextRankMismatch). A step mask that
mentions no iteration axis keeps rank 0 and an unchanged plan. Base-statement,
contracted and unbound mask axes stay refused at the source. The JAX bridge
refuses a step-aware axiswise node (axiswiseContextMask) until it supports one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
